DEVICE SPIKE

# Robot Lab: shift a two-speed gearbox and watch the output change speed.
# Model: Gearbox (motor A turns the input axle, motor B swings the changeover catch).
# The catch slides the driving ring onto one of two clutch gears. Only the gear the
# ring holds turns the output axle; the other one spins freely.
# Gear 1: the 8-tooth gear turns the 24-tooth gear, so the pointer turns 3 times slower.
# Gear 2: 16 teeth turn 16 teeth, so the pointer turns as fast as the motor.
WHEN flag clicked:
  set motor speed B 20
  set motor speed A 50
  display text "1"
  run motor B to position -26
  start motor A forward
  wait 4 seconds
  display text "2"
  run motor B to position 26
  wait 4 seconds
  display text "N"
  run motor B to position 0
  wait 3 seconds
  stop motor A
